Data files in this directory
============================

data/ko/starter.json
--------------------
Derived work.

  * Headwords and the 초급/중급/고급 grades come from
    julienshim/combined_korean_vocabulary_list, MIT licensed. The full licence
    text is in ../NOTICE, section 3.
  * The Vietnamese gloss on each entry is machine translation, produced by
    tools/build-korean-list.py. It is not edited by a person and carries no
    claim of accuracy.

Reuse it under the MIT terms in ../NOTICE.


data/zh/hsk.json
----------------
Derived work. Headwords, HSK 2.0 levels, pinyin and English meanings come
from drkameleon/complete-hsk-vocabulary, MIT licensed, built by
tools/zh/build-hsk-list.py. lang/zh/hsk.js is built from the same source. The
full licence text is in ../NOTICE, section 4.

Reuse it under the MIT terms in ../NOTICE.


data/zh/cedict.json
-------------------
Derived work, CC BY-SA 4.0. A trimmed CC-CEDICT (Simplified headwords, tone-
marked pinyin, up to three senses per reading), built by
tools/zh/build-cedict.py from CC-CEDICT as published by MDBG
(https://www.mdbg.net/chinese/dictionary?page=cc-cedict), itself based on
CEDICT, Copyright (C) 1997, 1998 Paul Andrew Denisowski. Licence:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ — see ../NOTICE, section 5.

Reuse it under CC BY-SA 4.0: credit CC-CEDICT and share alike.


data/en/*.json and data/decks.json
----------------------------------
The English word lists, built by tools/build-en-decks.py. Derived work,
CC BY-SA 4.0: credit the sources below and share alike.

  * Headwords and CEFR levels: CEFR-J Vocabulary Profile 1.5 (Tono Lab, TUFS)
    and the Octanove Vocabulary Profile C1/C2 (CC BY-SA 4.0). ../NOTICE,
    sections 7 and 8.
  * academic.json: the New Academic Word List 1.2 (CC BY-SA 4.0). ../NOTICE,
    section 9.
  * The topic of each word, the phrasal-verb bands, and every collocation,
    idiom, example sentence and Vietnamese meaning in collocations.json and
    idioms.json were written for this project (tools/en/*.tsv).
  * The Vietnamese gloss on the other entries is machine translation. It is
    not edited by a person and carries no claim of accuracy.

No definition, IPA or audio is included: the extension looks those up on your
machine the first time a word is shown.
data/decks.json is only an index of the folders in data/en, data/ko and data/zh.


What is NOT here
----------------
data/ielts-c1-c2.json and data/phrasal-verbs.json are not committed. Their
definitions, IPA, example sentences and audio links are Cambridge University
Press content, which this project has no right to redistribute. Build them on
your own machine with tools/build-ielts-list.py and tools/build-phrasal-list.py
— see the "Word lists" section of ../README.md.
